From: Armada <armada@armadaos.dev>
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno/a8xx: wait for ZPASS_DONE sample count writes

On the A830, DOOM (2016) with the OpenGL renderer hung the GPU consistently.
The hang needs occlusion queries and a fast GPU clock: a replay of the
hanging submit hung 5/5 at 1100 MHz and 0/6 at 160 MHz.

Turnip waits for the sample count write after an occlusion query ends
(emit_counter_barrier(): WFI, plus CP_BARRIER on A8xx). Freedreno has the
same helper but only uses it for pipeline statistics queries. Adding it
after the occlusion query end event, and after the autotune end event,
stopped the hang. Gameplay still hung every few seconds until the
end event that occlusion_resume() writes got the same wait.

Only A8xx gets the barrier, so other GPUs see no change.
---
diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a6xx/fd6_gmem.cc b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a6xx/fd6_gmem.cc
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a6xx/fd6_gmem.cc
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a6xx/fd6_gmem.cc
@@ -855,6 +855,12 @@
          .add(EV_DST_RAM_CP_EVENT_WRITE7_1(
             results_ptr(at, result[result->idx].samples_start)
          ));
+
+      /* See occlusion_pause(): wait for the sample count write on A8xx. */
+      if (CHIP >= A8XX) {
+         fd_pkt7(cs, CP_WAIT_FOR_IDLE, 0);
+         fd_pkt7(cs, CP_BARRIER, 1).add(1);
+      }
    }

    fd6_fence_write<CHIP>(cs, result->fence, results_ptr(at, fence));
diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a6xx/fd6_query.cc b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a6xx/fd6_query.cc
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a6xx/fd6_query.cc
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a6xx/fd6_query.cc
@@ -101,6 +101,10 @@
             .write_accum_sample_count_diff = true,
          ))
          .add(EV_DST_RAM_CP_EVENT_WRITE7_1(query_sample(aq, start)));
+
+      /* See occlusion_pause(). */
+      if (CHIP >= A8XX)
+         emit_counter_barrier<CHIP>(cs);
    }

    ctx->occlusion_queries_active++;
@@ -180,6 +184,12 @@
           * So we just give the start address in all cases.
           */
          .add(EV_DST_RAM_CP_EVENT_WRITE7_1(query_sample(aq, start)));
+
+      /* Like turnip, wait for the sample count write before going on. On
+       * A830 the CP hangs without it once the GPU clock is high enough.
+       */
+      if (CHIP >= A8XX)
+         emit_counter_barrier<CHIP>(cs);
    }

    assert(ctx->occlusion_queries_active > 0);
